  title={Streamlining Colorectal Cancer Classification using Synergistic SVM-InceptionV3 Approach}, 
  year={2026},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={1-6},
  abstract={Colorectal cancer is a major threat to health, underlining the need for proper diagnosis as the only way to get the best results. In the domain of medical imaging assessment, Convolutional neural network (CNN) models are already in use and showing some promising results, which is a big plus in this era of artificial intelligence. During this study, we intend to introduce an SVM-InceptionV3 CNN framework with the goal of improving the performance of image classification task. The InceptionV3 architecture is one of the new ways of dealing with image stratification and it is also good for both local and global aspect of features capturing. SVM integration makes our model efficient for image classification. In this research we have utilized publicly available Kvasir dataset and customized CRCCD-V1 dataset which were sourced from Sum Hospital, Odisha. We have obtained 94% accuracy with a test loss of 0.35 by very slightly modifying the InceptionV3 model. Thus, this research work brings in a new method for proper image categorization which can then improve the analysis of colorectal malignancy and in the long run, lead to more accurate reliable and accurate malignancy detection and improved medical prognoses. Besides, the development of AI and deep learning methods presents a great chance to enhance medical diagnosis and treatment planning.},
  keywords={Modeling;Printing;Cancer;Deep learning;Colorectal cancer;Support vector machines;Timing;Convolutional neural networks;Tumors;Signal detection;Colorectal Cancer;Image Classification;InceptionV3;Support Vector Machine (SVM);Synergistic Framework;and Medical Imaging;Customized CRCCD-V1 dataset;Deep Transfer Learning;Computer-Aided Diagnosis (CAD)},
