  title={Revolutionizing Oncology: AI Driven Approaches to Early Cancer Diagnosis}, 
  year={2025},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={1551-1557},
  abstract={The early detection of cancer such as ovarian, pancreatic, lung, breast and blood cancers are often left outstanding due to inaccurate traditional methods. This review studies research done to enhance the accuracy of early cancer diagnosis using AI techniques like deep learning, multi-omics data integration, imaging analysis. This report explores case studies based on breast cancer image classification and blood cancer profiling by using integrated genomic data which directly compares traditional cancer detection techniques with AI-driven advanced systems. Early detection and highly improved accuracy are found due to increased specificity and sensitivity thus making the results successful. The study emphasizes multimodal AI approaches for comprehensive analysis which combine a diverse data search. The results demonstrate potential in identifying biomarkers which prove to be an advantage by using the AI technology. These findings make it valuable for healthcare professionals by potentially reducing cancer detection times and increasing accuracy in the procedure in turn potentially reducing diagnostic errors and improving patient outcomes.},
