  abstract={Predicting the progression of liver cancer disease is a significant challenge in cancer research. In this study, we analyzed models for predicting the development of Hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) liver cancer. Due to its prevalence as a leading cause of liver cancer mortality, technological progress has resulted in the development of patients' data in various disease stages. Predicting HCC liver cancer using a publicly available dataset would necessitate assessing machine learning algorithms' prediction ability. We suggest employing machine learning methods like kNN, SVM, SGD, Neural Networks, Naïve Bayes, and Logistic regression. We calculate their area under the curve and assess its accuracy using real-world medical data on liver cancer. The experimental data demonstrates Neural Network gives superior performance.},
