  year={2024},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={344-351},
  abstract={This article aims to use machine learning to help improve the prediction of secondary primary thyroid cancer, although with advances in medicine, many previously unsolvable diseases can now be solved. However, due to the prolonged survival time of patients after treatment, the problem of cancer metastasis to other organs has not been well addressed. Based on this, we hope to combine machine learning frameworks with medical problems to help better address these issues. This article utilizes data from the SEER database from 2010 to 2015, which includes a total of 173633 thyroid cancer patients. Use multiple machine learning algorithms to predict the accuracy of the model. In order to improve prediction accuracy, we developed a stacked algorithm model that integrates decision tree (DT), multi-layer perceptron (MLP), logistic regression (LG), and selected logistic regression model as the second layer meta classifier. Optimize through feature weighting and raw data augmentation strategies. Our goal is to establish a scientific framework that can accurately diagnose and guide treatment decisions.},
